{"D:\\wt\\opalmites\\vlog\\opalmites\\voz\\b008_t5.wav": {"text": "Then the roost bars come down. Mine sit in brackets so they lift right out. And here's the part nobody does. I take a putty knife and an old stiff brush, and I scrape out every crack, every joint, every place where the roost bar sits in the bracket. That's where they live. Where two pieces of wood meet, that's where the eggs are. Then I scrub it all with hot soapy water and let it dry in the sun. If your roost bars are old and full of cracks, think about just replacing them. A new 8' 2x4 is about $5. I put new ones in this fall, and I rounded the top edges with a rasp so the hen's feet are comfortable. Fewer cracks, fewer places for mites to hide. Then the coop itself. I go over the walls and the nest boxes with the brush, especially along the edges and the corners.", "words": [{"w": " Then", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.18}, {"w": " the", "s": 0.18, "e": 0.4}, {"w": " roost", "s": 0.4, "e": 0.62}, {"w": " bars", "s": 0.62, "e": 0.92}, {"w": " come", "s": 0.92, "e": 1.22}, {"w": " down.", "s": 1.22, "e": 2.16}, {"w": " Mine", "s": 2.16, "e": 2.3}, {"w": " sit", "s": 2.3, "e": 2.56}, {"w": " in", "s": 2.56, "e": 2.74}, {"w": " brackets", "s": 2.74, "e": 3.24}, {"w": " so", "s": 3.24, "e": 3.44}, {"w": " they", "s": 3.44, "e": 3.62}, {"w": " lift", "s": 3.62, "e": 3.9}, {"w": " right", "s": 3.9, "e": 4.14}, {"w": " out.", "s": 4.14, "e": 5.04}, {"w": " And", "s": 5.04, "e": 5.14}, {"w": " here's", "s": 5.14, "e": 5.42}, {"w": " the", "s": 5.42, "e": 5.56}, {"w": " part", "s": 5.56, "e": 5.82}, {"w": " nobody", "s": 5.82, "e": 6.18}, {"w": " does.", "s": 6.18, "e": 7.18}, {"w": " I", "s": 7.34, "e": 7.44}, {"w": " take", "s": 7.44, "e": 7.7}, {"w": " a", "s": 7.7, "e": 7.86}, {"w": " putty", "s": 7.86, "e": 8.08}, {"w": " knife", "s": 8.08, "e": 8.48}, {"w": " and", "s": 8.48, "e": 8.62}, {"w": " an", "s": 8.62, "e": 8.78}, {"w": " old", "s": 8.78, "e": 8.98}, {"w": " stiff", "s": 8.98, "e": 9.32}, {"w": " brush,",